<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Jan forex reserves up at $1.356 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Jan forex reserves up at $1.356 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves rose to $1.356 billion in January from $1.182 billion in December, but were lower than $2.178 billion in January 1995, the State (central) Bank of Pakistan said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It gave no reason for the rise in the reserves, which it said included $466 million within Pakistan and $201 million held outside the country.</p>
<p>Following is the monthly foreign exchange reserves holdings position in Pakistan:</p>
<p>    (MLN DLRS)	    JAN	   DEC	   JAN 95</p>
<p>				1,356	1,182	    2,178</p>
<p> Forex in Pakistan	  466	  409	    1,153</p>
<p> Forex outside Pakistan   201	   84		306</p>
<p> Gold coins and bullion   676	  676		705</p>
<p> Special Drawing Rights    13	   13		 14</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
